# a + b of two BigInts is one call, which may allocate and may throw. Both go in as cells and a cell comes back.
# CHECK-LABEL: name="add" role=Source
# CHECK-NEXT: BB#0:
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[a]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[b]] = ArgumentReg(
# CHECK-NEXT: Int64 b@[[sum]] = Patchpoint(b@[[a]]:Register({{*}}), b@[[b]]:Register({{*}}), resultConstraints = Register({{*}}), ExitsSideways|{{*}}:Add)
# CHECK-NEXT: Return(b@[[sum]], Terminal)
# CHECK-LABEL: end of function
# No path for numbers stands in front of the call: nothing tests what the operands are.
# NONE-LABEL: name="add" role=Source
# NONE-NOT: Branch(
# NONE-NOT: Double
# NONE-NOT: Int32
# NONE-LABEL: end of function
# The callee is the stub for sums of any two values behind the test for two 32-bit integers.
# CALLS: f1:
# CALLS-NEXT: stub BinaryOperation.AddAfterInt32Check x1
